  "content": {
    "id": "p42-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Divide these polynomials and write in the form $P(x)=D(x)Q(x)+R(x)$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p42-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$(x^3+x^2-2x+3)\\div(x-1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^3+x^2-2x+3=(x-1)(x^2+2x)+3$",
          "worked": "Long division gives quotient terms $x^2$ and $2x$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x^3+x^2-2x+3)-x^2(x-1)&=2x^2-2x+3\\\\(2x^2-2x+3)-2x(x-1)&=3\\\\Q(x)&=x^2+2x\\\\R(x)&=3\\\\x^3+x^2-2x+3&=(x-1)(x^2+2x)+3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p42-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(3x^3-x^2+x+2)\\div(x+1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3x^3-x^2+x+2=(x+1)(3x^2-4x+5)-3$",
          "worked": "Long division gives quotient terms $3x^2$, $-4x$ and $5$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(3x^3-x^2+x+2)-3x^2(x+1)&=-4x^2+x+2\\\\(-4x^2+x+2)-(-4x)(x+1)&=5x+2\\\\(5x+2)-5(x+1)&=-3\\\\Q(x)&=3x^2-4x+5\\\\R(x)&=-3\\\\3x^3-x^2+x+2&=(x+1)(3x^2-4x+5)-3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p42-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$(x^3-x^2+2x+1)\\div(x+1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^3-x^2+2x+1=(x+1)(x^2-2x+4)-3$",
          "worked": "Long division gives quotient terms $x^2$, $-2x$ and $4$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x^3-x^2+2x+1)-x^2(x+1)&=-2x^2+2x+1\\\\(-2x^2+2x+1)-(-2x)(x+1)&=4x+1\\\\(4x+1)-4(x+1)&=-3\\\\Q(x)&=x^2-2x+4\\\\R(x)&=-3\\\\x^3-x^2+2x+1&=(x+1)(x^2-2x+4)-3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p42-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$(x^4-3x^2+x-2)\\div(x-1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^4-3x^2+x-2=(x-1)(x^3+x^2-2x-1)-3$",
          "worked": "Include $0x^3$ in the dividend. Long division gives quotient terms $x^3$, $x^2$, $-2x$ and $-1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x^4+0x^3-3x^2+x-2)-x^3(x-1)&=x^3-3x^2+x-2\\\\(x^3-3x^2+x-2)-x^2(x-1)&=-2x^2+x-2\\\\(-2x^2+x-2)-(-2x)(x-1)&=-x-2\\\\(-x-2)-(-1)(x-1)&=-3\\\\Q(x)&=x^3+x^2-2x-1\\\\R(x)&=-3\\\\x^4-3x^2+x-2&=(x-1)(x^3+x^2-2x-1)-3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
      },
      {
        "id": "p43-part-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$(x^3-x+1)\\div(x+2)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^3-x+1=(x+2)(x^2-2x+3)-5$",
          "worked": "Include $0x^2$ in the dividend. Long division gives quotient terms $x^2$, $-2x$ and $3$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x^3+0x^2-x+1)-x^2(x+2)&=-2x^2-x+1\\\\(-2x^2-x+1)-(-2x)(x+2)&=3x+1\\\\(3x+1)-3(x+2)&=-5\\\\Q(x)&=x^2-2x+3\\\\R(x)&=-5\\\\x^3-x+1&=(x+2)(x^2-2x+3)-5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
      {
        "id": "p43-part-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$(x^3+x^2-3)\\div(x-1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^3+x^2-3=(x-1)(x^2+2x+2)-1$",
          "worked": "Include $0x$ in the dividend. Long division gives quotient terms $x^2$, $2x$ and $2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x^3+x^2+0x-3)-x^2(x-1)&=2x^2-3\\\\(2x^2+0x-3)-2x(x-1)&=2x-3\\\\(2x-3)-2(x-1)&=-1\\\\Q(x)&=x^2+2x+2\\\\R(x)&=-1\\\\x^3+x^2-3&=(x-1)(x^2+2x+2)-1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
      {
        "id": "p43-part-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$(x^4-2)\\div(x+3)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^4-2=(x+3)(x^3-3x^2+9x-27)+79$",
          "worked": "Include the missing terms with zero coefficients. Long division gives quotient terms $x^3$, $-3x^2$, $9x$ and $-27$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x^4+0x^3+0x^2+0x-2)-x^3(x+3)&=-3x^3-2\\\\(-3x^3+0x^2+0x-2)-(-3x^2)(x+3)&=9x^2-2\\\\(9x^2+0x-2)-9x(x+3)&=-27x-2\\\\(-27x-2)-(-27)(x+3)&=79\\\\Q(x)&=x^3-3x^2+9x-27\\\\R(x)&=79\\\\x^4-2&=(x+3)(x^3-3x^2+9x-27)+79\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 82
      },
      {
        "id": "p43-part-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$(x^4-x^2)\\div(x-4)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^4-x^2=(x-4)(x^3+4x^2+15x+60)+240$",
          "worked": "Include the missing terms with zero coefficients. Long division gives quotient terms $x^3$, $4x^2$, $15x$ and $60$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x^4+0x^3-x^2+0x+0)-x^3(x-4)&=4x^3-x^2\\\\(4x^3-x^2+0x+0)-4x^2(x-4)&=15x^2\\\\(15x^2+0x+0)-15x(x-4)&=60x\\\\60x-60(x-4)&=240\\\\Q(x)&=x^3+4x^2+15x+60\\\\R(x)&=240\\\\x^4-x^2&=(x-4)(x^3+4x^2+15x+60)+240\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 82
      }
    ]
